WEBVTT

00:00:01.116 --> 00:00:03.088
Welcome to Lead Velocity.

00:00:03.088 --> 00:00:04.905
You've paid for your first cycle,

00:00:04.905 --> 00:00:07.405
so here's exactly what happens next:

00:00:07.405 --> 00:00:10.137
how your leads reach you, where your money goes,

00:00:10.137 --> 00:00:12.381
and how the results get better over time.

00:00:13.875 --> 00:00:15.576
First, we get you set up.

00:00:15.576 --> 00:00:19.970
We check your FSP number on the public FSCA register.

00:00:19.970 --> 00:00:23.656
You connect your calendar, add your photo and a short bio,

00:00:23.656 --> 00:00:25.808
and give us your business WhatsApp number.

00:00:25.808 --> 00:00:28.372
Once your payment has cleared and that's done,

00:00:28.372 --> 00:00:32.305
your campaigns go live, normally within three business days.

00:00:33.736 --> 00:00:37.293
Our ads run under our consumer brand, SortMyCover.

00:00:37.293 --> 00:00:39.741
They never name a product or a price.

00:00:39.741 --> 00:00:43.079
Someone taps an ad, answers a few quick questions,

00:00:43.079 --> 00:00:44.960
and agrees to be contacted.

00:00:44.960 --> 00:00:47.808
Our WhatsApp assistant follows up within minutes,

00:00:47.808 --> 00:00:49.548
introduces you by name,

00:00:49.548 --> 00:00:51.868
practice and FSP number,

00:00:51.868 --> 00:00:54.393
and books a time straight into your calendar.

00:00:54.393 --> 00:00:55.953
They confirm they'll attend,

00:00:55.953 --> 00:00:59.935
and only then does that person count as one of your Qualified Leads.

00:00:59.935 --> 00:01:02.602
You get a WhatsApp and a short pre-call brief.

00:01:02.602 --> 00:01:06.043
We send them reminders right up to ten minutes before the meeting.

00:01:06.043 --> 00:01:08.674
After that, the conversation is yours.

00:01:10.136 --> 00:01:11.115
On Bronze,

00:01:11.115 --> 00:01:15.226
you pay sixteen thousand five hundred rand for a thirty-day cycle.

00:01:15.226 --> 00:01:17.288
We plan for just over half of that,

00:01:17.288 --> 00:01:19.621
about eight and a half thousand rand,

00:01:19.621 --> 00:01:22.301
to go straight into advertising on Meta.

00:01:22.301 --> 00:01:24.144
That's the biggest single part.

00:01:24.144 --> 00:01:26.889
The rest runs everything around the ads:

00:01:26.889 --> 00:01:29.840
the WhatsApp assistant, booking and reminders,

00:01:29.840 --> 00:01:32.417
the creative, the testing and tracking,

00:01:32.417 --> 00:01:35.252
and the people doing the work. It's a flat fee.

00:01:35.252 --> 00:01:38.811
It's never linked to policies, premiums or commission.

00:01:40.270 --> 00:01:42.332
We never set it and forget it.

00:01:42.332 --> 00:01:45.889
We test a few genuinely different ads side by side,

00:01:45.889 --> 00:01:48.994
usually for at least a week, before we pick a winner.

00:01:48.994 --> 00:01:52.242
We watch the numbers every day: cost per lead,

00:01:52.242 --> 00:01:55.412
how many people book, and how many actually show up.

00:01:55.412 --> 00:01:57.783
When people have seen an ad too often,

00:01:57.783 --> 00:02:01.585
results get more expensive, so we keep refreshing the creative.

00:02:01.585 --> 00:02:05.554
Meta's system usually needs about fifty results in a week to settle,

00:02:05.554 --> 00:02:08.713
so we make changes on purpose, not on impulse.

00:02:10.196 --> 00:02:12.206
Here's what makes it better over time.

00:02:12.206 --> 00:02:13.611
When a person attends,

00:02:13.611 --> 00:02:16.884
and they've said yes to ad measurement, we tell Meta.

00:02:16.884 --> 00:02:19.745
That shows the system who your real clients look like,

00:02:19.745 --> 00:02:21.162
not just who clicked.

00:02:21.162 --> 00:02:23.624
Once we have at least a hundred of those people,

00:02:23.624 --> 00:02:26.021
Meta can build a lookalike audience:

00:02:26.021 --> 00:02:28.405
new people who share their characteristics.

00:02:28.405 --> 00:02:30.905
It works better with a thousand or more,

00:02:30.905 --> 00:02:32.399
which is why we pool what we learn

00:02:32.399 --> 00:02:35.080
across all the advisers we work with.

00:02:35.080 --> 00:02:39.139
At around twenty a month, this is a slow build, not a switch.

00:02:39.139 --> 00:02:42.503
Lookalikes are available for these ads in South Africa today,

00:02:42.503 --> 00:02:44.139
but Meta can change that,

00:02:44.139 --> 00:02:47.425
so we treat them as a bonus, never a promise.

00:02:47.425 --> 00:02:49.603
And we never target anyone by health,

00:02:49.603 --> 00:02:52.118
income or other sensitive traits.

00:02:53.570 --> 00:02:54.807
Your part is simple.

00:02:54.807 --> 00:02:56.560
Keep your calendar up to date.

00:02:56.560 --> 00:02:57.964
After every meeting,

00:02:57.964 --> 00:03:00.645
tap one button to tell us whether they attended.

00:03:00.645 --> 00:03:03.699
That tap is the signal that improves your leads.

00:03:03.699 --> 00:03:06.431
If someone doesn't show, wait ten minutes,

00:03:06.431 --> 00:03:08.441
then send us your proof straight away.

00:03:08.441 --> 00:03:11.794
We may replace them as goodwill, up to three a week.

00:03:13.283 --> 00:03:14.043
That's it.

00:03:14.043 --> 00:03:17.304
We'll handle the ads, the follow-up and the bookings.

00:03:17.304 --> 00:03:18.837
You do what you do best.

00:03:18.837 --> 00:03:20.733
Welcome to Lead Velocity.
